# The lab and CI are Linux while the author develops on Windows, so a checkout
# must not rewrite line endings and hand Linux a CRLF file. Store every text
# file with LF and check it out with LF on every platform. This matters most
# for anything run or parsed byte for byte: a shell script with CRLF fails its
# shebang on Linux, and a recorded tool-output fixture (docs/rules/test.md)
# must match what the tool really emits. Binary files are detected by
# `text=auto` and left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
